course: dictionary
lesson: 11463
title: Adopted: taken as your own
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word adopted can have more than one meaning. Read the words around it to find out which one fits. «Mia was adopted when she was two, and she is loved by her family.» Here adopted means that she became a full member of her family by law, even though she was not born into it.
explain: «We adopted a puppy from the shelter last week.» Here adopted means taken as your own. The clues are puppy and shelter: people bring a pet home from a shelter and care for it as their own. Ask yourself: does the sentence show someone taking something or someone into their life?
explain: Adopted can also be the past tense of the verb adopt. «Our class adopted a tiger at the zoo by paying for its food.» Adopted means chose and started to support or look after. Swap in a simple word such as chose: if it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Adopted means taken as your own.
fact: An adopted child has become, by law, a full member of a family they were not born into.
fact: Pets can be adopted from animal shelters.
fact: Adopted is also the past form of the verb adopt: adopt, adopts, adopted, adopting.
fact: How someone joined their family is a private story, and an adopted child is as much part of the family as any other child.
exercise: «Sam was adopted by a kind couple when he was a baby.» What does adopted mean here? | Born in a hospital | Ran away from home | *Became a full member of a family he was not born into | Lost his way
exercise: «The school adopted a new rule about phones.» What does adopted mean? | Broke | *Chose and started to use | Threw away | Forgot about
exercise: «Priya's adopted country is Canada.» What does adopted country suggest? | A country she was born in | *A country she chose and has made her own | A country with no people | A country on a map she drew
test: «We adopted a kitten from the animal shelter on Monday.» What does adopted mean? | *Taken home as our own | Painted | Sold at the shop | Left behind
test: Which word is the past form of adopt? | adopting | adopts | *adopted | adopt
exam: «Ben's adopted brother is a year older than him.» What does adopted brother mean? | A brother Ben chose from a list | A brother who lives far away | A brother who is a twin | *A brother who joined Ben's family by law but was not born into it
